# data-models-relationships

Core data models and their relationships focus on tracking inmates, cases, agents and location records for bail compliance monitoring.

Key Entity Relationships:

1. Inmate Records
- Associated with multiple cases
- Linked to bond records and compliance checks
- Contains identification and contact information 
- Maps to geographic monitoring boundaries

2. Case Management 
- Links inmates to active warrants
- Associates cases with jurisdictions
- Tracks bond/bail status
- Records compliance requirements

3. Location Verification
- Ties check-in records to specific cases
- Stores geographic coordinates with accuracy radius
- Links to photo verification entries
- Maintains compliance audit trail

4. Agent Management
- Maps agents to jurisdictions
- Links to case assignments
- Tracks contact sequences
- Associates with verification reviews

5. Bond Records
- Connects inmates to active bonds
- Tracks monetary amounts and conditions
- Links to compliance schedules
- Associates with specific jurisdictions

Importance Score: 90/100
- Critical data models supporting core bail monitoring functionality
- Complex relationships between inmates, cases, locations and compliance
- Domain-specific schemas for legal/regulatory requirements
- Multi-jurisdiction data partitioning

